# ========================================================== target_plane.parm - target fixed-wing
# (gazebo-plane6 / stars-plane)
# ============================================================================ Loading chain:
# gazebo-plane.parm, THIS FILE (probe). Content moved from bumblebee/params/target.parm; The
# measurements there are valid. ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1) TECS_SYNAIRSPEED 1 - Required for AUTO/GUIDED speed commands to take effect. ARSPD_TYPE 0
# (fdm.airspeed is always 0 because Gazebo does not call backend Aircraft::update_dynamics()). AP_TECS
# chooses the path without airspeed while SYNAIRSPEED 0; DO_CHANGE_SPEED (178) The aircraft remains at
# trim speed even if ACK=ACCEPTED is returned. Measurement (bumblebee, 2026-07-25): syn=0 -> command
# 10/15/18/22 m/s, realized ALL 20.2; syn=1 -> 9.93 / 15.01 / 17.93 / 21.98.
TECS_SYNAIRSPEED 1

# 2) AIRSPEED_CRUISE 20 - ArduPlane 4.7 TRIM_ARSPD_CM in gazebo-plane.parm is now an invalid name; If
# not written, factory 12 m/s remains.
AIRSPEED_CRUISE 20

# 3) AHRS_WIND_MAX 1 - trims synthetic airspeed error. IAS = |V_gps(NED) - W_EKF3| / Since EAS2TAS is
# produced, the only source of error is EKF3 wind forecast and cannot be observed in the straight leg.
# Without clipping, the ground speed can be 22.05 while keeping IAS 20.
AHRS_WIND_MAX 1

# 4) ARSPD_TYPE 0 - The validity of (1) and (3) depends on this; for clarity.
ARSPD_TYPE 0
